  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maximizing efforts to control and eliminate Malaria in Somalia - Somalia (01-Jan-2024-31-Dec-2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia, Malaria, United Nations Children&apos;s Fund (UNICEF)This program has the following goals: attain zero malaria death and reduce malaria incidence to at least 0.5/1000 population by 2026. This is to be achieved through four overarching strategic pillars and objectives.. The objectives of this program are: &#x201c;By 2026, Atleast 95% of population at risk of malaria living in accessible areas are provided with appropriate malaria prevention and case management services&#x201d;.  &#x201c;By 2026, at least 20 districts shall be reporting zero local transmission of malaria&#x201d;..  &#x201c;By 2026, malaria M&amp;E, EPR and surveillance capacity is enhanced to provide the required national strategic information for decision making&#x201d;..  &#x201c;By 2026, the enabling environment and systems for malaria response in Somalia are optimally functioning&#x201d;.</narrative>
  </description>
